VPRune research release

This repository isolates the final training-free VPRune method. Its core
code is extracted/adapted from the project's local research implementation,
not a verbatim copy of all official CDPruner baseline code.

Algorithmic attribution:
* Visual-only DPP uses the cosine Gram kernel employed by CDPruner, with
  its text-relevance conditioning removed. Greedy incremental Cholesky
  MAP inference follows Chen et al. (2018). DPP is not claimed as new.
* Position preservation follows Grounding-Aware Token Pruning (GAP).
  Original position IDs are not claimed as a new positional embedding.
* Similarity-guided recycling assigns discarded features to nearest
  retained features and applies group-softmax convex fusion. Similarity
  means feature-space similarity, not guaranteed spatial adjacency.

